    section4Title: "What's included and how pricing works",
    section4Body: "Pricing for doorstep turban tying in Mombasa is built from four main factors: the fabric chosen, the total number of safas needed, the complexity of the fold or style, and how far the team needs to travel. A simple, single groom booking with a standard fold costs less than a full wedding party package with a premium fabric and detailed accessory work, so there isn't one fixed number that applies to every enquiry — it genuinely depends on what you need. What's included in every booking, regardless of package size, is the artist's time, styling expertise, and coordination of the tying schedule around your ceremony timing; fabric can either be supplied as part of the package or, if your family already has fabric selected, we can quote for tying alone. Accessories like a kalgi, brooch or pearl detailing are usually priced separately from the base tying service, since not every booking needs them. The fastest way to get an accurate number is to share your date, venue, total headcount and any fabric preferences together — we'll come back with a package that reflects your actual event rather than a generic estimate.",
