    section3Body: "People searching for wedding pagdi tying price in Nakuru are usually at one of two points in their planning: either they have a firm date and venue and are now filling in the remaining vendor bookings, or they're still in an earlier research phase, comparing a few options before committing to anything. Both are completely fine starting points — we can give a useful answer either way, whether that's a full package quote or just a general sense of pricing and availability for your rough dates. A meaningful share of these enquiries also come from wedding planners managing several vendors for one client, in which case we're glad to communicate directly with the planner rather than requiring the couple's involvement in every message. If you're not the person getting married — a parent, sibling or friend helping with arrangements — that's common too, and the process works the same way, just with a note to loop in the groom or couple once style and colour decisions need finalising.",
